# lumen configuration schema — DOCUMENTATION ONLY.
# Real values live in OpenBao at kv/data/lumen/{env}, rendered into the pod env
# by ExternalSecrets (INFRA §5). Committing a VALUE here or anywhere is a
# doctrine break; this file lists KEYS and their meaning.
#
# The machine-readable source of the per-role key set is the code itself:
#   lumen config keys --role admin | cms | all
# prints exactly the names that role BINDS (the binding table in
# internal/config is the single source — this file mirrors it for humans).

# ---- PROCESS ROLES (owner ruling 2026-11-13, the role split) ----
#
# ONE binary, LUMEN_ROLE selects the plane:
#
#   admin  lumen-admin (foundation plane). CONTROL PLANE ONLY: session
#          mint (/admin/session — the ONLY place tokens are born), the NEW
#          /admin/session/verify door other planes introspect through,
#          whoami/logout/password, users CRUD, the TOFU setup wizard (the
#          users table is admin's), and the §9 Bao relay. Its database
#          (lumen_admin) holds ONLY the users/session-lineage tables.
#          NO content routes, NO queue/worker, NO public /api reads,
#          NO media relay, NO Meilisearch.
#   cms    lumen-staging / lumen-production. CONTENT PLANE: the §1 public
#          reads (/api/*), the admin content desks (posts/photos/tags/
#          collections/media), the index worker queue. Auth on every desk
#          request is INTROSPECTED against the admin plane
#          (LUMEN_ADMIN_URL → POST /admin/session/verify), cached ~30 s
#          keyed by token hash — revocation propagates ≤30 s later at the
#          desk edge (session TTL semantics live in DESIGN §8); an
#          unreachable admin plane FAILS CLOSED with 503 "admin plane
#          unreachable". No users table, no login, no mint, no relay.
#          Trust note: the verify call forwards the bearer AS-IS with no
#          extra shared secret — the path is ClusterIP-only (lumen has no
#          public ingress, INFRA §2) and the admin plane holds the real
#          auth decision.
#   all    UNSET DEFAULT — the legacy single-process dev plane: every
#          surface, local JWT auth, both key families bound. Dev plane and
#          tests keep working unchanged; "all" is NEVER a cluster posture
#          (the deployments set admin or cms explicitly).
#
#   LUMEN_ROLE              admin | cms | all (unset = all, legacy dev).

# ---- Runtime env (12-factor: the process reads its environment, never a
#      file; precedence env > env.yaml > default) ----
#
# SHARED KEYS (both planes):
#   LUMEN_DB_URL      postgres:// connection string. The cluster wires one
#                     per plane: Patroni lumen_admin (admin) / lumen (cms).
#   PORT | LUMEN_PORT HTTP listen port (default 8080; PORT is the workspace
#                     container convention, LUMEN_PORT wins when both set;
#                     the unrouted admin/metrics port stays separate per
#                     the observability contract).
#   LUMEN_CONFIG      explicit env.yaml path (dev comfort only).
#
# ADMIN-PLANE KEYS ONLY (cms processes do NOT bind these — a leaked value
# in a cms pod env is read by nothing, structurally):
#   LUMEN_SESSION_JWT_SECRET  HS256 key, 32 random bytes, generated at
#                     bootstrap — Bao lumen/{env}. The signing key is
#                     ADMIN-ONLY by ruling (2026-11-13): the cms plane
#                     mints nothing and must not hold it.
#   LUMEN_BAO_ADDR | LUMEN_BAO_ROLE_ID | LUMEN_BAO_SECRET_ID
#                     the §9 relay's AppRole door (also what driftcheck and
#                     `config check-epoch` read as CI verbs). Consumed by
#                     internal/bao directly; absent = the /admin/bao
#                     surface honestly does not exist.
#
# CMS-PLANE KEYS ONLY:
#   LUMEN_ADMIN_URL   base URL of the admin plane (cluster DNS, e.g.
#                     http://lumen-admin:8080) — REQUIRED for `server`:
#                     desk bearers are introspected against it (see the
#                     role block above for the cache/fail-closed rules).
#   LUMEN_MEILI_URL   Meilisearch service (the read path, §4) — required
#                     on this plane; the admin plane never dials it.
#   LUMEN_MEILI_KEY   engine master key (dev placeholder in compose; Bao).
#   LUMEN_MEILI_INDEX_POSTS   posts index uid, default "posts" (dev
#                     unchanged). Honored by EVERY engine call, the worker/
#                     server bootstrap, and the seed.
#   LUMEN_MEILI_INDEX_PHOTOS  photos index uid, default "photos". (The tags
#                     index name stays the constant "tags" — the ruling
#                     enumerates posts/photos only.)
#   LUMEN_MEDIA_ENDPOINT, LUMEN_MEDIA_REGION, LUMEN_MEDIA_BUCKET,
#   LUMEN_MEDIA_ACCESS_KEY, LUMEN_MEDIA_SECRET_KEY, LUMEN_MEDIA_CDN_BASE,
#   LUMEN_MEDIA_FORCE_PATH
#                     the §5 object relay (GATE #9 CLOSED 2026-11-13:
#                     provider Cloudflare R2, S3-compatible; seed shape per
#                     runbook/05–06). Uploads are a cms-desk surface — the
#                     admin plane does not bind these at all.
#   LUMEN_MEDIA_PREFIX  object-key prefix, default "". Applied ONCE at the
#                     upload site so ALL puts AND the returned URL
#                     composition share base+prefix+key: the bucket (or
#                     CDN space) can host several planes/tenants with
#                     separate key spaces (e.g. "staging") while keys stay
#                     content-addressed under the prefix. Empty = the old
#                     shape byte-for-byte; the stored photo src and the
#                     media_assets ledger row carry the prefixed key, so
#                     GC and dedupe stay exact.
#   LUMEN_MEDIA_CREATE_BUCKET
#                     dev-only escape hatch (prod never auto-creates).
#   LUMEN_ORIGIN      absolute base for feed URLs/redirects (prod:
#                     https://gofar.id) — a public-read concern, so it
#                     rides the cms plane.
#
# CLI-ONLY (never a server binding, not in `config keys`):
#   LUMEN_PASSWORD    the `lumen user` bootstrap verb (admin-plane DB);
#                     the password never travels in argv.
